1
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:41,067
All pirates searching for the treasure One Piece must brave the second half of the Grand Line.

2
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:46,067
These wild and dangerous seas are known as the New World.

3
00:02:46,067 --> 00:02:52,067
Gold Roger and his crew were the only men to ever chart these waters and learn all the secrets they held.

4
00:02:52,067 --> 00:03:00,067
For the rest of the pirates of the world, this has proven to be the end of the road, a graveyard of dreams.

5
00:03:00,067 --> 00:03:09,067
Now, Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body became rubber after eating the gum gum fruit, sets sail into the New World with his faithful crew.

6
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:13,067
I'm gonna be the king of the pirates!

7
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:19,067
It's been two years since the War of the Best in Marineford.

8
00:03:19,067 --> 00:03:24,067
Scattered across the world, Luffy and his crew underwent special training to prepare for the trials ahead.

9
00:03:24,067 --> 00:03:31,067
Now, after taming the terrors of the deep, they have finally made their way to Fishman Island, thousands of feet below sea level.

10
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:34,067
Listen up, guys!

11
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:41,067
Let's go!

12
00:03:41,067 --> 00:03:46,067
How about I give you an option?

13
00:03:46,067 --> 00:03:50,067
Enlist under our banner as members of the new Fishman Pirates.

14
00:03:50,067 --> 00:03:52,067
Or else...

15
00:03:52,067 --> 00:03:55,067
Or else meaning we sink you right now!

16
00:03:55,067 --> 00:03:57,067
Yeah, right, you wish!

17
00:03:57,067 --> 00:03:59,067
Stupid!

18
00:03:59,067 --> 00:04:01,067
Here goes...

19
00:04:01,067 --> 00:04:03,067
Coo-de-burst!

20
00:04:03,067 --> 00:04:06,067
This bubble...

21
00:04:06,067 --> 00:04:07,067
It's a double structure!

22
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:10,067
We're about to run into another bubble!

23
00:04:10,067 --> 00:04:11,067
You guys ready?

24
00:04:13,067 --> 00:04:14,067
Water?

25
00:04:20,067 --> 00:04:22,067
This current is really strong!

26
00:04:22,067 --> 00:04:23,067
Crap!

27
00:04:23,067 --> 00:04:32,067
Four of us can't swim!

28
00:04:39,067 --> 00:04:40,067
Come on!

29
00:04:41,067 --> 00:04:42,067
Reach!

30
00:04:44,067 --> 00:04:45,067
Nami!

31
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:46,067
Robin!

32
00:04:49,067 --> 00:04:50,067
Dammit!

33
00:04:50,067 --> 00:04:52,067
I can't resist the current!

34
00:05:03,067 --> 00:05:04,067
Where am I?

35
00:05:04,067 --> 00:05:05,067
Oh, Luffy-chin!

36
00:05:07,067 --> 00:05:09,067
It's been a while, hasn't it?

37
00:05:11,067 --> 00:05:13,067
This is a coral apartment complex.

38
00:05:13,067 --> 00:05:15,067
The dorms are at the very bottom, so rinse cheap.

39
00:05:15,067 --> 00:05:18,067
The top floor is the most expensive because it gets natural light.

40
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:20,067
It's the surface!

41
00:05:20,067 --> 00:05:21,067
We made it!

42
00:05:22,067 --> 00:05:23,067
Hey!

43
00:05:23,067 --> 00:05:24,067
K-me!

44
00:05:25,067 --> 00:05:26,067
Hey, guys!

45
00:05:27,067 --> 00:05:28,067
Huh?

46
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:30,067
Finally!

47
00:05:31,067 --> 00:05:34,067
I found my all blue after all these years!

48
00:05:38,067 --> 00:05:39,067
Interesting.

49
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:43,067
So Straw Hat finally made it to our turf, did he?

50
00:05:43,067 --> 00:05:44,067
Good for him.

51
00:05:44,067 --> 00:05:47,067
Well, what are we gonna do about it, boss?

52
00:05:50,067 --> 00:05:52,067
I want you to bring him here.

53
00:05:53,067 --> 00:05:54,067
And quickly.

54
00:05:58,067 --> 00:05:59,067
Excitement Blowout!

55
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,067
Sanji's life under threat!

56
00:06:00,067 --> 00:06:14,067
The Straw Hats are human, they can't breathe down here.

57
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:17,067
Assuming they're still alive, there aren't many places they can go.

58
00:06:18,067 --> 00:06:20,067
Guess we should head for town, huh?

59
00:06:20,067 --> 00:06:21,067
No.

60
00:06:21,067 --> 00:06:23,067
Wherever they are, they can't hide from Lord.

61
00:06:39,067 --> 00:06:40,067
Well, great.

62
00:06:40,067 --> 00:06:41,067
Okay, now what should I do?

63
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:46,067
It's hard to believe I'm so far under water.

64
00:06:51,067 --> 00:06:52,067
Huh?

65
00:06:52,067 --> 00:06:53,067
Huh?

66
00:07:08,067 --> 00:07:11,067
Super...

67
00:07:12,067 --> 00:07:13,067
Landing.

68
00:07:14,067 --> 00:07:15,067
Hey, Nami.

69
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:16,067
Whew, glad you made it out okay.

70
00:07:17,067 --> 00:07:18,067
Yeah? No thanks to you!

71
00:07:18,067 --> 00:07:21,067
You almost gave me a heart attack, you big dummy!

72
00:07:22,067 --> 00:07:23,067
Robin!

73
00:07:25,067 --> 00:07:26,067
Robin.

74
00:07:27,067 --> 00:07:28,067
Hey.

75
00:07:28,067 --> 00:07:29,067
Nami?

76
00:07:30,067 --> 00:07:31,067
You alright?

77
00:07:31,067 --> 00:07:32,067
Is this...

78
00:07:32,067 --> 00:07:33,067
Fishman Island?

79
00:07:34,067 --> 00:07:35,067
Yeah, probably.

80
00:07:35,067 --> 00:07:37,067
Frankie's scouting out the area to figure that out.

81
00:07:38,067 --> 00:07:40,067
Hmm? Back in the land of the living?

82
00:07:42,067 --> 00:07:43,067
So it seems.

83
00:07:43,067 --> 00:07:44,067
Find anyone else?

84
00:07:45,067 --> 00:07:46,067
Nope.

85
00:07:46,067 --> 00:07:47,067
They're all thrown in different directions.

86
00:07:48,067 --> 00:07:49,067
Geez.

87
00:07:49,067 --> 00:07:50,067
We just got back together again, too.

88
00:07:51,067 --> 00:07:53,067
Eh, we'll find them sooner or later.

89
00:07:53,067 --> 00:07:56,067
They're tough suckers, so I'm sure they're doing fine wherever they are.

90
00:07:57,067 --> 00:07:58,067
He does have a point.

91
00:07:58,067 --> 00:08:01,067
No offense to the crew, but I'm more worried about the sunny.

92
00:08:01,067 --> 00:08:04,067
I'm hoping the locals might have heard some news about our big crash.

93
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:06,067
I saw a town right around the corner.

94
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:08,067
Huh?

95
00:08:08,067 --> 00:08:09,067
Huh?

96
00:08:09,067 --> 00:08:10,067
Ha ha!

97
00:08:11,067 --> 00:08:12,067
Ha ha ha ha!!

98
00:08:13,067 --> 00:08:14,067
Conti!?

99
00:08:15,067 --> 00:08:16,067
Alright, here I come!

100
00:08:18,067 --> 00:08:20,067
This is it!

101
00:08:23,067 --> 00:08:24,067
This is my new.

102
00:08:25,067 --> 00:08:26,067
Home!

103
00:08:27,067 --> 00:08:29,067
usa.

104
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:34,327
He isn't spewing blood everywhere, so I guess he's better now.

105
00:08:34,987 --> 00:08:35,907
I don't get it.

106
00:08:36,067 --> 00:08:38,027
This sucks. I want to swim, too.

107
00:08:38,167 --> 00:08:40,387
You can. All we have to do is get you a bubble.

108
00:08:40,867 --> 00:08:41,547
Oh, really?

109
00:08:41,867 --> 00:08:44,707
Uh-huh. We can have one made in the city. Sound good?

110
00:08:44,887 --> 00:08:45,267
Yeah!

111
00:08:45,547 --> 00:08:46,607
This is a lucky break.

112
00:08:47,027 --> 00:08:50,527
If he had a nosebleed now, we wouldn't be able to do a transfusion.

113
00:08:51,027 --> 00:08:53,227
Sanji's blood type is rare, and we're all out.

114
00:08:53,367 --> 00:08:55,987
What? That sounds like seriously bad news.

115
00:08:56,227 --> 00:08:57,107
Hey, Kami?

116
00:08:57,667 --> 00:08:57,947
Huh?

117
00:08:57,947 --> 00:09:02,707
While I'm here, there's somebody I'd really like to see if we can find them somehow.

118
00:09:03,027 --> 00:09:05,327
Oh? Don't tell me. The Mermaid Princess?

119
00:09:05,747 --> 00:09:09,027
Nope. It's Jinbei.

120
00:09:11,087 --> 00:09:12,867
They call him Boss down here.

121
00:09:13,227 --> 00:09:16,727
Wait. When you say Jinbei, you're talking about the Warlord Jinbei?

122
00:09:17,367 --> 00:09:20,687
Or, I mean, former Warlord, since he resigned after the whole war thing.

123
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,487
Yeah. He's a good friend of mine.

124
00:09:22,527 --> 00:09:24,847
Huh? Him and the Pirate Empress?

125
00:09:24,987 --> 00:09:27,667
You make some weird friends when we're not around.

126
00:09:27,667 --> 00:09:31,307
When Ace died two years ago, I had a tough time pulling it together.

127
00:09:31,627 --> 00:09:35,547
In fact, I doubt I'd even be here right now, if it wasn't for his help.

128
00:09:35,747 --> 00:09:37,467
I've had enough of your nonsense!

129
00:09:37,467 --> 00:09:45,147
Boy, you can't see a thing. You're blind.

130
00:09:45,147 --> 00:09:51,907
What's gone may be gone, but you still have something left in this world to treasure, don't you?

131
00:09:51,907 --> 00:10:05,547
I still have my crew!

132
00:10:05,547 --> 00:10:08,507
I can't wait to talk to him again!

133
00:10:08,507 --> 00:10:16,187
See you on Fishman Island in two years! Be sure to bring your entire crew along! I look forward to meeting everyone!

134
00:10:16,187 --> 00:10:19,827
He said to meet here, and there's no way I'm gonna let him down!

135
00:10:19,827 --> 00:10:25,787
Now that you mention it, I heard he went to Marineford with you when you rang that bell and everyone got all worked up!

136
00:10:25,787 --> 00:10:27,707
Yahoo!

137
00:10:27,707 --> 00:10:32,707
You know where we can find him?

138
00:10:32,707 --> 00:10:37,667
Well, it's kind of tricky, because Boss doesn't exactly live on the island with everyone else.

139
00:10:37,667 --> 00:10:38,667
Huh?

140
00:10:38,667 --> 00:10:42,667
Since he resigned from the Warlords, they have to treat him like a normal pirate again.

141
00:10:42,667 --> 00:10:47,547
That means all the Fishman Pirates can't stay in the city anymore, so they found a new place to live.

142
00:10:47,547 --> 00:10:51,067
It's not too far from here, but that's where you'll have to go if you want to see him.

143
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:54,547
What? That sounds like a pain. This place has some dumb rules.

144
00:10:54,547 --> 00:11:00,667
I know it seems weird, but even though we're all the way down here, the War of the Best ended up affecting us, too.

145
00:11:00,667 --> 00:11:04,507
Kamee! Kamee! Kamee! Kamee! Kamee! Kamee!

146
00:11:04,507 --> 00:11:05,507
Huh?

147
00:11:05,507 --> 00:11:07,307
There's a big ship coming!

148
00:11:07,307 --> 00:11:08,987
Kamee! It's a ship from the palace!

149
00:11:08,987 --> 00:11:10,507
Yeah, but maybe nobody's on it.

150
00:11:10,507 --> 00:11:12,507
Don't be stupid. Of course someone is.

151
00:11:12,507 --> 00:11:14,987
So did you see somebody on the ship or not?

152
00:11:14,987 --> 00:11:16,187
No, not yet.

153
00:11:16,187 --> 00:11:19,907
But it was for sure the royal family ship. They don't usually come around here.

154
00:11:19,907 --> 00:11:23,947
Maybe they've come here to arrest Luffy because he didn't enter the city the right way.

155
00:11:23,947 --> 00:11:25,187
So what if they do?

156
00:11:25,187 --> 00:11:25,707
Huh?

157
00:11:25,707 --> 00:11:27,907
You guys had better hide before they get here.

158
00:11:27,907 --> 00:11:28,907
Huh?

159
00:11:28,907 --> 00:11:29,407
Huh?

160
00:11:29,407 --> 00:11:30,987
Sanji, quick, this way.

161
00:11:30,987 --> 00:11:32,487
Yeah!

162
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:41,807
She's right. That ship's the royal gondola.

163
00:11:41,807 --> 00:11:42,587
I thought so.

164
00:11:42,587 --> 00:11:43,087
I knew.

165
00:11:43,087 --> 00:11:43,587
Maybe.

166
00:11:43,587 --> 00:11:45,087
Totally. So what?

167
00:11:45,087 --> 00:11:48,747
Even so, I doubt anyone from the royal family is actually riding on it.

168
00:11:48,747 --> 00:11:52,307
This corner of the island's sort of out of the way for them, so they don't usually bother.

169
00:11:53,947 --> 00:12:10,187
Attention, all citizens! The three Neptune brothers have arrived!

170
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:15,947
Greetings, ladies of the cove. I hope that you can answer an inquiry of mine.

171
00:12:15,947 --> 00:12:17,947
Ahh! The princess are here!

172
00:12:17,947 --> 00:12:19,507
That's me! Anything!

173
00:12:19,507 --> 00:12:20,507
That princess?

174
00:12:22,987 --> 00:12:23,987
Sanji, no!

175
00:12:28,787 --> 00:12:30,187
Hide here and stay still.

176
00:12:30,187 --> 00:12:35,427
What is this feeling? Marshmallow, maybe?

177
00:12:35,427 --> 00:12:47,647
No, it's too big for that. But it has such a sweet smell. Intoxicating like some forbidden fruit. Yet too soft to be a melon. Too warm.

178
00:12:47,647 --> 00:12:49,687
Hey, what are...

179
00:12:49,687 --> 00:12:50,687
Ahh!

180
00:12:50,687 --> 00:12:51,687
Ahh!

181
00:12:51,687 --> 00:12:53,007
Ahh!

182
00:12:53,007 --> 00:12:53,687
Ahh!

183
00:12:53,687 --> 00:12:54,687
Ahh!

184
00:12:54,687 --> 00:12:55,687
Ahh!

185
00:12:55,687 --> 00:12:56,687
Ahh!

186
00:12:56,687 --> 00:12:57,687
Ahh!

187
00:12:57,687 --> 00:12:58,687
Ahh!

188
00:12:58,687 --> 00:13:04,127
I received a report that someone entered the city illegally. Have they come by here, perhaps?

189
00:13:04,127 --> 00:13:09,127
If they have, and you've seen them, be sure to tell me if I saw Latina!

190
00:13:10,127 --> 00:13:16,127
Mumbo, mumbo, shiki shiki moonfish, why we gotta do this? Let's party with the ladies!

191
00:13:16,127 --> 00:13:18,127
I'm sorry, but we haven't seen anyone here.

192
00:13:18,127 --> 00:13:21,127
They sound like common thugs. Are they really that important?

193
00:13:21,127 --> 00:13:25,127
Surely they don't demand the attention of princes such as you.

194
00:13:25,127 --> 00:13:30,127
Perhaps. We have yet to ascertain their identities, so it may be too early to say just yet.

195
00:13:30,127 --> 00:13:32,127
He doesn't know! Latina!

196
00:13:32,127 --> 00:13:38,127
Who cares? Let's dance! Yay! Ain't nobody nothing about nobody!

197
00:13:44,127 --> 00:13:46,127
What's all this commotion?

198
00:13:46,127 --> 00:13:50,127
Oh man, it's the princess from Neptune's army!

199
00:13:50,127 --> 00:13:53,127
What are they doing here? What a pain in the ass.

200
00:13:53,127 --> 00:13:55,127
Now what?

201
00:13:55,127 --> 00:13:58,127
Let's see how it plays out.

202
00:13:58,127 --> 00:14:00,127
Mumbo, mumbo, shiki!

203
00:14:00,127 --> 00:14:05,127
Ah, I see. Well, I thank you all. We shall search elsewhere.

204
00:14:06,127 --> 00:14:08,127
Forgive me for interrupting your leisure.

205
00:14:08,127 --> 00:14:11,127
We'll dance again sometime!

206
00:14:11,127 --> 00:14:13,127
And away we go! Latina!

207
00:14:13,127 --> 00:14:15,127
Bye-bye!

208
00:14:15,127 --> 00:14:18,127
Perhaps the border guards were just seeing things!

209
00:14:19,127 --> 00:14:21,127
They're leaving...

210
00:14:21,127 --> 00:14:25,127
So soft...

211
00:14:25,127 --> 00:14:27,127
So soft...

212
00:14:27,127 --> 00:14:28,127
And...

213
00:14:28,127 --> 00:14:29,127
Pink...

214
00:14:29,127 --> 00:14:30,127
Soft...

215
00:14:30,127 --> 00:14:32,127
Pink...

216
00:14:32,127 --> 00:14:33,127
Squishy...

217
00:14:33,127 --> 00:14:35,127
Fuffy!

218
00:14:35,127 --> 00:14:38,127
Ooh, ooh, what is that?

219
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:40,127
Aw, crap, Sanji!

220
00:14:46,127 --> 00:14:48,127
Oh, what did I do?

221
00:14:48,127 --> 00:14:51,127
That was too much blood! He needs help now!

222
00:14:51,127 --> 00:14:54,127
He's done for! All that pent-up lust let loose in one shot!

223
00:14:54,127 --> 00:14:56,127
Sanji!

224
00:14:57,127 --> 00:15:00,127
Wait, no mistaking it.

225
00:15:00,127 --> 00:15:03,127
That's the pirate's straw hat Luffy.

226
00:15:05,127 --> 00:15:09,127
Mom-o-nights, go!

227
00:15:09,127 --> 00:15:11,127
Yes, sir!

228
00:15:35,127 --> 00:15:39,127
What a pain!

229
00:15:39,127 --> 00:15:41,127
Everything here looks the same.

230
00:15:41,127 --> 00:15:44,127
I could be walking in circles for all I know.

231
00:15:54,127 --> 00:15:58,127
You're Roro Noah Zoro from the Straw Hat Pirates, right?

232
00:15:58,127 --> 00:16:04,127
Yeah, so what if I am?

233
00:16:09,127 --> 00:16:12,127
Well, look at that. How convenient.

234
00:16:12,127 --> 00:16:14,127
I don't know, the gods are gonna catch him first.

235
00:16:14,127 --> 00:16:18,127
Our orders are clear, but we don't want to start crap with the Neptune army.

236
00:16:22,127 --> 00:16:24,127
Wait, hold on a second, please!

237
00:16:24,127 --> 00:16:26,127
We don't want to fight! We can sort out our crimes later!

238
00:16:26,127 --> 00:16:28,127
But right now there's an emergency!

239
00:16:28,127 --> 00:16:31,127
Our friend has lost a lot of blood and we need a donor, quick!

240
00:16:31,127 --> 00:16:35,127
If you leave him here or throw him in jail, he'll be dead within an hour!

241
00:16:36,127 --> 00:16:38,127
His blood type is SRH negative.

242
00:16:38,127 --> 00:16:41,127
I know it's rare, but does someone here have it? Anyone?

243
00:16:42,127 --> 00:16:45,127
Fishmen and humans do have the same kind of blood, don't they?

244
00:16:46,127 --> 00:16:47,127
Chopper chin.

245
00:16:47,127 --> 00:16:50,127
We don't have time! Guys, this is serious!

246
00:16:50,127 --> 00:16:53,127
Sanchi, we are not losing you over this!

247
00:16:54,127 --> 00:16:56,127
Please, I'm begging you! Whatever it takes!

248
00:16:57,127 --> 00:16:59,127
I can't let my friend die!

249
00:17:00,127 --> 00:17:01,127
Chopper chin, I'm sorry.

250
00:17:02,127 --> 00:17:06,127
Fishmen and humans do have the same kind of blood, but the situation is complicated.

251
00:17:07,127 --> 00:17:08,127
The thing is...

252
00:17:08,127 --> 00:17:10,127
Hammo, Hammo, Hammo, Hammo!

253
00:17:10,127 --> 00:17:12,127
Hammo, Hammo, Hammo, Hammo!

254
00:17:13,127 --> 00:17:15,127
Get a load of these humans!

255
00:17:15,127 --> 00:17:17,127
You really are stupid, aren't you?

256
00:17:18,127 --> 00:17:21,127
Weren't you a big enough jerk the last time we met?

257
00:17:21,127 --> 00:17:24,127
His name is Hammond, sir. He's from the Fishmen District.

258
00:17:25,127 --> 00:17:27,127
Hammo, Hammo, Hammo!

259
00:17:27,127 --> 00:17:30,127
You're not getting a damn drop from anybody on this island!

260
00:17:31,127 --> 00:17:33,127
Why would we share our blood with disgusting creatures like you?

261
00:17:33,127 --> 00:17:35,127
Humans aren't worth a thing down here!

262
00:17:35,127 --> 00:17:42,127
And even if someone did help you, decent fishmen like us who hate humans would make sure they were punished for it.

263
00:17:43,127 --> 00:17:44,127
Punished?

264
00:17:45,127 --> 00:17:49,127
He can bleed out right here for all I care. Many fishmen would happily watch him die.

265
00:17:50,127 --> 00:17:54,127
There's a law for this, you know. One we've followed for a long time.

266
00:17:55,127 --> 00:17:58,127
Fishmen are forbidden to share blood with humans no matter what.

267
00:17:59,127 --> 00:18:00,127
That law sucks!

268
00:18:00,127 --> 00:18:01,127
Don't blame me for it.

269
00:18:01,127 --> 00:18:05,127
After all, it was humans who set the rule in the first place.

270
00:18:06,127 --> 00:18:11,127
Our blood may be the same, but for ages you've treated us like monsters or worse, like animals.

271
00:18:11,127 --> 00:18:13,127
Your blood was too good for us!

272
00:18:14,127 --> 00:18:18,127
In fact, that's why Fisher Tiger, the hero of this island, died.

273
00:18:20,127 --> 00:18:22,127
He said that name once before.

274
00:18:22,127 --> 00:18:32,127
He fought to free slaves of all races, and when that battle took its toll on his body, when he lied bloody and battered, not a single human would offer their blood to return his kindness.

275
00:18:32,127 --> 00:18:37,127
A transfusion would have saved him, but because of humans, he died!

276
00:18:40,127 --> 00:18:43,127
So right now, you have but one choice.

277
00:18:44,127 --> 00:18:50,127
Well, it's not much of a choice really. Your friend is going to die and you're coming to the Fishman District with me.

278
00:18:50,127 --> 00:18:56,127
Horty Jones, the captain of the new Fishman Pirates, is expecting you, and he doesn't like to wait.

279
00:18:57,127 --> 00:18:58,127
That's enough!

280
00:18:59,127 --> 00:19:05,127
Hey, who cares about some stupid rule in the first place? You don't have to listen to this thug! There's someone's life on the line here!

281
00:19:06,127 --> 00:19:11,127
We'll do anything it takes to repay you! Now is not the time to get stuck on pride!

282
00:19:11,127 --> 00:19:15,127
What? Would you give it up already?

283
00:19:17,127 --> 00:19:18,127
Kimmy!

284
00:19:18,127 --> 00:19:19,127
Come along, straw hat!

285
00:19:20,127 --> 00:19:21,127
Now, second gear!

286
00:19:24,127 --> 00:19:26,127
I'll take you by force if I have to!

287
00:19:27,127 --> 00:19:28,127
Troll!

288
00:19:29,127 --> 00:19:31,127
I'm not joining your stupid crew!

289
00:19:32,127 --> 00:19:33,127
I already told you, didn't I?

290
00:19:34,127 --> 00:19:35,127
John Pesso!

291
00:19:36,127 --> 00:19:37,127
Leave us alone!

292
00:19:41,127 --> 00:19:47,127
Get away! The thing is too big!

293
00:19:56,127 --> 00:19:58,127
My word, he made quick work of them.

294
00:19:59,127 --> 00:20:02,127
It just gave up! I guess Luffy can tame sea monsters now?

295
00:20:03,127 --> 00:20:06,127
What happened? That was crazy!

296
00:20:07,127 --> 00:20:08,127
Impressive.

297
00:20:08,127 --> 00:20:10,127
Luffy-chan, up here!

298
00:20:11,127 --> 00:20:17,127
Bring Sanji-chan up here! We'll go back to town!

299
00:20:18,127 --> 00:20:19,127
The Ryugu is moving.

300
00:20:20,127 --> 00:20:23,127
There's lots of humans there, so we might be able to find a blood donor! Let's hurry!

301
00:20:24,127 --> 00:20:25,127
I'm coming!

302
00:20:25,127 --> 00:20:26,127
Cool! Ready to go! Thanks, Kimmy!

303
00:20:26,127 --> 00:20:30,127
Sure! We need to head over to town. Is that okay?

304
00:20:30,127 --> 00:20:31,127
Mason!

305
00:20:31,127 --> 00:20:32,127
Mason!

306
00:20:32,127 --> 00:20:33,127
Hey! You can't do that! It belongs to the princess!

307
00:20:33,127 --> 00:20:34,127
I'm sorry, guys! We'll bring your ship back as soon as we save Sanji-chan!

308
00:20:34,127 --> 00:20:39,127
And away they go! How are we supposed to get home now? So-la-ti-do!

309
00:20:39,127 --> 00:20:48,127
Hmph!

310
00:20:48,127 --> 00:20:57,127
It's not fair. I'd do anything in the world to save his life, but I don't have the right-

311
00:20:57,127 --> 00:21:00,747
Oh, how are we supposed to get home now, so la-ti-do?

312
00:21:04,687 --> 00:21:09,907
It's not fair. I'd do anything in the world to save his life, but I don't have the right blood type.

313
00:21:09,987 --> 00:21:12,047
No, it's nothing for you to feel bad about.

314
00:21:12,447 --> 00:21:15,507
If he wasn't such a perv, this wouldn't have happened in the first place.

315
00:21:15,967 --> 00:21:19,067
Look at him. He's dying, and he's still thinking about boobs.

316
00:21:19,067 --> 00:21:23,687
So bouncy. So soft and bouncy and so soft and bouncy.

317
00:21:23,687 --> 00:21:29,827
Stop! You're in a delicate state! If you keep thinking about dirty stuff, you're going to lose what little blood you have left!

318
00:21:31,607 --> 00:21:37,867
We may be friends, but considering the way you and Hachi got treated back on Saba-Odi, I should have guessed something like this would happen.

319
00:21:38,167 --> 00:21:40,327
There's some deep-rooted stuff going on here.

320
00:21:40,887 --> 00:21:46,447
Yeah, and to be honest, I don't know how this will go. There's no promise anyone will help us back in town.

321
00:21:47,827 --> 00:21:52,367
We're counting on human donors for blood, but I haven't seen any at all this past month.

322
00:21:52,367 --> 00:21:55,587
In fact, your ship is the first one we've had in a long time.

323
00:21:55,767 --> 00:21:58,327
Why? I thought everyone had to come through here.

324
00:21:58,487 --> 00:22:00,107
Yeah, it wasn't like this before.

325
00:22:00,827 --> 00:22:05,967
Nobody can say for certain, but we think someone's attacking the travelers, like what happened with you guys.

326
00:22:06,207 --> 00:22:10,467
There's something going on in this kingdom, and I have a sinking feeling it's about to get ugly.

327
00:22:14,207 --> 00:22:16,447
Please, ladies, you must be forthright.

328
00:22:17,107 --> 00:22:19,607
Why did you try to conceal those pirates from us?

329
00:22:19,607 --> 00:22:23,567
We're sorry, Prince. They aren't bad people.

330
00:22:23,787 --> 00:22:26,087
It sounds like what happened wasn't their fault.

331
00:22:26,287 --> 00:22:31,687
They're Kami's friends, and they got split up from their crew, so we didn't want them to be thrown in jail as soon as they got here.

332
00:22:31,727 --> 00:22:32,607
Don't be sad!

333
00:22:32,747 --> 00:22:34,667
I hope they find a donor for Sanji.

334
00:22:35,007 --> 00:22:36,687
Alas, you misunderstood us.

335
00:22:37,007 --> 00:22:38,687
Their method of entry is no concern.

336
00:22:39,327 --> 00:22:40,167
They're quite famous.

337
00:22:40,667 --> 00:22:42,207
It would only be a small formality.

338
00:22:42,567 --> 00:22:44,567
We don't consider them enemies, after all.

339
00:22:44,567 --> 00:22:47,487
Yeah, we had different business with them.

340
00:22:47,687 --> 00:22:49,067
Re mi fa sol la ti!

341
00:22:50,447 --> 00:22:52,187
Then this is all our fault.

342
00:22:54,747 --> 00:22:58,707
We had a message to pass on to them, from Jinbei.

343
00:22:58,707 --> 00:23:13,047
Sanji's love for mermaids has turned from a harmless obsession into a life-threatening disaster.

344
00:23:13,507 --> 00:23:18,247
Luffy and his friends take him to the Mermaid Cafe to rest, but they must find a blood donor soon.

345
00:23:18,787 --> 00:23:23,527
Later, Kami introduces them to Madam Charlie, owner of the cafe and expert fortune teller.

346
00:23:23,887 --> 00:23:27,507
Unfortunately, it seems that she only sees destruction in Luffy's future.

347
00:23:27,507 --> 00:23:31,527
On the next, One Piece, the Fishman Island will be annihilated!

348
00:23:31,967 --> 00:23:33,027
Charlie's prophecy!

349
00:23:33,467 --> 00:23:35,147
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

